+# SOCC final-section check: maintenance-record lock-out request, unjoined labels and planned closure
+
+October 31, 2026. Existing operational-record tasks TEL02/TEL04 and recorder provenance dependency REC01 remain open. This source comparison supplements the [informal-log/message-transfer lead](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/blob/deb98709a44079e1ad5ddb0b62bc814b6ef30c60/investigation/broader-evidence/socc-record-targets-2026-10-31/README.md). It does not replace the technical owner's recorder analysis or authenticate a recorder/aircraft association.
+
+The final log section supplies a dated **maintenance-record control contact** and a **planned closing conference**. Neither establishes completed preservation, successful recording retrieval or a completed lessons-learned review.
+
+## Source observations kept separate
+
+| Exact mirror locator | Source report / manual reading | Limit and next record |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| [Viewer page 27](https://www.scribd.com/document/16762194/T7-B20-Timelines-9-11-2-of-2-Fdr-AA-SOCC-Log-Redacted-Version#page=27), SEPT21 divider, row **10:35**, AA KEAN COMM **002556** | Corporate communications sought flight segments from September 6 for flights 11 and 77; the row calls its labels tail numbers and reads **334 (11)** and **5BP (77)**. The phrase from September 6 does not establish a one-day-only range. It reports unavailability in DECS/TDEC and a commercial-system check/callback | This is a reported information request and pending lookup, not the underlying segment extract, registry mapping or completed result |
+| [Viewer page 29](https://www.scribd.com/document/16762194/T7-B20-Timelines-9-11-2-of-2-Fdr-AA-SOCC-Log-Redacted-Version#page=29), row **1854**, before the September 22 divider, AA KEAN COMM **002558** | Reports that maintenance records were still open for **334 and BBP**, and that FOS Control was contacted for lock-out | The actual records, asset mapping, system definition, request, audit log, success/failure and retained copy remain unacquired. Date context follows page27's September21 divider; no new date header beside this row |
+| [Viewer page 31](https://www.scribd.com/document/16762194/T7-B20-Timelines-9-11-2-of-2-Fdr-AA-SOCC-Log-Redacted-Version#page=31), September24 divider, row **0840**, AA KEAN COMM **002560** | A closing conference was planned for that day at **1000** | Planning is not attendance, minutes, closure approval or the actual informal lessons-learned log |
+
+The **5BP / BBP** contrast is preserved without a preferred replacement. Page27 explicitly associates its 5BP label with flight77; page29 does not itself identify BBP as flight77 or demonstrate that the two rows refer to the same second asset. A differing field/asset, transcription or another source-description problem are untested possibilities. The shared 334 label and surrounding context suggest a candidate join, not proof of identity. The original fleet-to-registration and maintenance-record crosswalk is needed before calling this a contradiction about one aircraft. No aircraft substitution is inferred.
+
+One higher-zoom view of each entry supported these readings. The initial lower-resolution page27 glyph looked S-shaped/uncertain; it is recorded as **our reading uncertainty**, not invented as a third historical value. No source bytes, labels or masks were corrected. The row ordering on page29 also remains as displayed: 1857 appears above 1854; neither is silently reordered into an authenticated chronology.
+
+## What this changes, and what it does not
+
+The maintenance entry provides a specific control point to trace: FOS Control, the two displayed asset labels, the dated request and its execution/audit trail. It records a contact for lock-out, not proof that data were frozen, copied, preserved, deleted or later supplied. The applicable system terminology and meaning of open/lock-out remain unverified. Maintenance records are also not automatically flight-recorder configuration, raw recorder input or recorder custody documentation.
+
+The planned September24 conference narrows the search for closure/debrief materials following the earlier September17 informal-log announcement. Page32 contains a closing-message fragment, not a demonstrated conference record or full unredacted message. The relevant source body on page31 is masked; its contents cannot be inferred. The later retrospective account of an after-action event remains a separate source, not proof that this planned conference occurred or used that log.
+
+These entries report information-seeking and record-control/review activity. They are relevant contrary evidence to blanket claims that no effort was made; actual execution and effectiveness remain unknown. No concealment, motive, coordination or conspiracy is established by the label contrast, a pending lookup, masked text or a missing outcome.
+
+In the readable regions of **pages25–32**, no explicit disposition of the earlier recording-retrieval request, native recording identifier, transfer/receipt, actual informal log or completed closure/debrief record was found. This is a bounded reading, not proof that such records never existed or a complete reading of all32pages. Earlier pages13–18remain only partly inspected.
+
+## Scope, verification and unfinished work
+
+Twenty browser images were inspected: eighteen initial regions covering pages25–32, plus two higher-zoom label details within the prospective cap. Native PDF/source entity and its SHA-256 remain **unknown**. These manual notes are not original-page captures or a substitute source hash. The mirror is not joined to the [known NARA file unit2608461](https://catalog.archives.gov/id/2608461) by a page-level release manifest.
+
+Two new source-specific searches sought the FOS lock-out/maintenance chain after checking prior query holdings. They returned no relevant original in the displayed results; unrelated modern FOS/mining content was not used as evidence or opened. No native original, applicable system rule, fleet crosswalk or audit result was acquired. Search failure does not establish nonexistence, withholding or destruction.
+
+[READING-SCOPE.json](READING-SCOPE.json) records exact scope and reading uncertainty. [SOURCE-PINS.json](SOURCE-PINS.json) preserves the distinct source assertions; [OPEN-TODOS.json](OPEN-TODOS.json) specifies discriminating inputs. All eighteen original-input requirements remain open or partial; no new native-data/scientific test or substantive criterion was completed. [CHECKLIST.md](CHECKLIST.md), the editorial [EDITORIAL-REVISION.diff](EDITORIAL-REVISION.diff), and the real Git addition [TEXT-CHANGES.diff](TEXT-CHANGES.diff) record revision accountability. The editorial revision qualifies our date-range shorthand without changing either source label. Source/layout reading and text diff are separate checks.
+
+Only original research notes are published. Raw scans/screenshots, identifying/contact/access fields, other marked material, private correspondence, case strategy and credentials are excluded. Sources, prior reports, conflicting records and TODOs remain unchanged. No outreach, fee, new request/filing, private push, deletion, merge or history rewrite occurred. AveLyra publication and remote verification are recorded separately; publication does not complete the underlying investigation.
